      "text": "Your plan to learn n8n by watching how someone else structures a real workflow, starting with webhooks and credentials, is a sound way to learn it. \n The closest thing I have is a self-hosted n8n workflow for a missed-call text-back. A signed Twilio-style voice webhook hits n8n, which verifies the X-Twilio-Signature, builds the text-back and sends it through a Twilio node. It then logs the miss to a Supabase table. Bad signatures get a 403, and Twilio errors go to a separate error-log branch. It’s test-built on localhost with SMS suppressed, so it isn’t in production. \n The same pattern shows up in a CSV import workflow I built: upload, allow-list the columns, validate, dedupe, then report inserted and skipped rows. \n Since you already test POST requests, I’d start in two steps: \n(1) Move from ReqBin to signed requests, so you see why signature checks and replay protection matter. \n(2) Add an error branch to one of your workflows, so failures get logged instead of vanishing. \n I can walk you through the exported workflow JSON on a live screen-share, node by node, and explain why each piece is where it is.",
